        "note": "Use-after-free in the librsvg bundled with sharp's prebuilt libvips (librsvg 2.62.91 in @img/sharp-libvips-* 1.3.3). Fixed in 0.35.5, which ships librsvg 2.63.2 and libvips 8.18.7 (@img/sharp-libvips-* 1.3.4). The exact apps/api pin moves from 0.35.4 to 0.35.5; astro's optional ^0.35.4 and the webpack minimizer's optional peer resolve to the same single version, without an override. Exposure before the fix: the API image pipeline admits only JPEG/PNG/WebP signatures, re-checks the decoded format, and decodes only in a child process that requires VIPS_BLOCK_UNTRUSTED=1, under which libvips rejects SVG input (measured on both 0.35.4 and 0.35.5); the renderer does not use astro:assets. No product path decoded SVG, but the vulnerable binaries shipped in the runtime image."
